    "https://wooster.edu/employment/jobs": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Bagpipes, Part-Time",
      "description": "Jobs <img  height=\"1\" width=\"1\" style=\"display:none\" src=\"https://www.facebook.com/tr?id=637525146410015&amp;ev=PageView&amp;noscript=1\"> Skip to content Close Future Students Current Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Explore Academics Library Areas of Study Meet the Faculty Independent Study Student Success About Wooster About the College Campus Life News & Updates Athletics Visit & Apply Admissions Apply Visit Wooster Financial Aid Connect Employment Campus Events Wooster Magazine SEARCH Apply Give Future Students Current Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Explore Academics Library Areas of Study Meet the Faculty Independent Study Student Success About Wooster About the College Campus Life News & Updates Athletics Visit & Apply Admissions Apply Visit Wooster Financial Aid Connect Employment Campus Events Wooster Magazine Apply Give Academics Library Areas of Study Meet the Faculty Independent Study Student Success About Wooster About the College Campus Life News & Updates Athletics Visit & Apply Admissions Apply Visit Wooster Financial Aid Connect Employment Campus Events Wooster Magazine Career Opportunities Employment Career Opportunities Creative Dining Important Links All FACULTY STAFF All FACULTY STAFF Adjunct Instructor of Bagpipes, Part-Time Teach weekly bagpipe lessons, coach Pipe Band musicians, maintain instruments, and collaborate with Scottish arts instructors. VIEW JOB DETAILS VIEW JOB DETAILS Adjunct Instructor of Flute Part-time position for a flute instructor beginning August 2026. Primary duties include teaching weekly flute lessons to both majors and non-majors, as well as coaching ensemble(s) as needed. VIEW JOB DETAILS VIEW JOB DETAILS Adjunct Instructor of Scottish Drumming, Part-Time Teach weekly Scottish drumming lessons, coach Pipe Band musicians, maintain instruments, and collaborate with bagpipe and Highland dance instructors. VIEW JOB DETAILS VIEW JOB DETAILS Bus Driver, Part-Time The Transportation Services Driver provides safe and reliable transportation services for the College community by operating buses, shuttles, and service vehicles. VIEW JOB DETAILS VIEW JOB DETAILS Finance Director of Strategy and Long Range Planning The Finance Director of Strategy and Long-Range Planning is responsible for providing advanced financial guidance, deploying capital strategically, and leading financial initiatives and decision support. VIEW JOB DETAILS VIEW JOB DETAILS General Maintenance Technician Under general supervision, performs a variety of general maintenance duties, including mechanical, carpentry, and construction work, to maintain and repair college facilities, property, and equipment. VIEW JOB DETAILS VIEW JOB DETAILS Manager of Equipment Operations & Assistant Coordinator of Facilities and Events The Manager of Equipment Operations / Assistant Coordinator of Facilities and Events oversees all aspects of the athletic equipment room servicing the College's 23 varsity sports and intramural programming and is an important member of the facility and event operations team... VIEW JOB DETAILS VIEW JOB DETAILS Senior Accountant, Grants and General Ledger The Senior Accountant, Grants and General Ledger is responsible for the accounting, administration and financial oversight of all College grants; primarily federal research grants and private grants from corporations and foundations. VIEW JOB DETAILS VIEW JOB DETAILS Shuttle Driver, Part-Time The Shuttle Driver provides safe, reliable, and customer-focused transportation services for college students, employees, and guests. VIEW JOB DETAILS VIEW JOB DETAILS Student Care and Support Coordinator The Student Care and Support Coordinator serves as a key member of the Dean of Students office, providing individualized assistance to students and connecting them with campus and community resources... VIEW JOB DETAILS VIEW JOB DETAILS Video and Multimedia Production Manager The Video and Multimedia Producer leads the creation of compelling, distinctive, and inspiring branding video, audio, and motion graphic content that tells the story of the College. VIEW JOB DETAILS VIEW JOB DETAILS Independent Minds, Working Together Admissions Wooster Admissions Apply Now Request Info Visit Campus Financial Aid Academics Areas of Study Library Independent Study Meet the Faculty Student Success Campus Life Living on Campus Athletics Resources Fast Facts Campus Map Current Student Portal Faculty & Staff Portal About Wooster About the College Mission & Values Leadership News Employment Framing Our Future © 2026 The College of Wooster. All rights reserved. Privacy Policy Terms of Use Disclaimer Title IX Non-Discrimination Policy"
