te timely passenger pick-up and drop-off services while maintaining adherence to established transportation schedules. Assist passengers with entering and exiting vehicles, providing accommodations as needed. Load, unload, and handle passenger luggage and personal belongings in a safe and courteous manner. Operate vehicles in compliance with all applicable traffic laws, safety regulations, and College policies. Maintain accurate trip records and complete required documentation in accordance with College procedures. Exercise professionalism, discretion, and sound judgment while representing the College. Deliver exceptional customer service by fostering a welcoming, responsive, and positive transportation experience for passengers. Other duties as assigned Requirements: Education and/or Experience: High school diploma or general education degree (GED). Five years related experience as a professional driver. SKILLS: Ability to apply commonsense understanding to carry out instructions furnished in written, oral, or diagram form. Ability to deal with problems involving several concrete variables in standardized situations. Ability to read and interpret documents such as safety rules, operating and maintenance instructions, maps, and procedure manuals. Ability to write routine reports and correspondence. Ability to converse effectively with visitors, guests, or staff members of the College. KNOWLEDGE: Ability to add, subtract, multiply, and divide in all units of measure, using whole numbers, common fractions, and decimals ABILITIES: Acknowledge and comply with all departmental SOP, safety, and college requirements. Commitment to COW's mission, vision and values. Additional Information: The College of Wooster does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, sex/gender, gender identity, gender expression, medical condition, political affiliation, religion, creed, ethnicity, national origin (including ancestry), citizenship status, disability, age, marital status, family 