    "https://wooster.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203275": {
      "title": "The College of Wooster \n\tJob Posting: Student Care and Support Coordinator",
      "description": "The College of Wooster\nJob Posting: Student Care and Support Coordinator The College of Wooster \n\tJob Posting: Student Care and Support Coordinator Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Student Care and Support Coordinator Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Student Affairs Locations: Wooster, OH Posted: Aug 3, 2026 Closes: Sep 27, 2026 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: Full-time Exempt Position ID: 203275 Share About The College of Wooster: Wooster offers an excellent, comprehensive liberal arts education, culminating in a rigorous senior project, in which each student works one-on-one with a faculty mentor to conceive, organize and complete a significant research project on a topic of the student's own choosing. Through this distinctive program, every Wooster student develops abilities valued by employers and graduate schools alike: independent judgment, analytical ability, creativity, project-management and time-management skills, and strong written and oral communication skills. Founded in 1866, the college enrolls approximately 2,000 students. The College offers a comprehensive benefits program that includes: Health, Dental, Retirement, and Tuition Remission for eligible positions. Job Description: Summary: The Student Care and Support Coordinator serves as a key member of the Dean of Students office, providing individualized assistance to students and connecting them with campus and community resources that promote personal well-being, academic success, and persistence. This position coordinates care referrals, assists students in navigating support services, and collaborates with faculty, staff, and community partners to address barriers that may impact student success. The Coordinator works proactively to identify students in need of support, facilitate resource referrals, and follows up with students to ensure they have access to the services and assistance needed to achieve their educational goals. Essential Departmental Duties and Responsibilities: Student Support and Care Coordination Serve as a point of contact for students experiencing personal, academic, behavioral, or other challenges. Receive, review, and respond to student care referrals from faculty, staff, and students. Assess student needs and connect students with appropriate campus and community resources. Provide individualized support and follow-up to ensure students successfully access recommended services. Maintain accurate and confidential records of student interactions, referrals, and outcomes. Resource Navigation Assist students in identifying and accessing available support services, including: Academic support and tutoring Mental health and counseling resources Accessibility and disability services Financial aid and emergency assistance Food, housing, and basic-needs support Health and wellness resources Career services and workforce development programs Develop and maintain knowledge of campus and community resource networks. Create resource materials and educational content to increase awareness of student support services. Collaboration and Outreach Partner with faculty, staff, and administrators to support students of concern and promote student well-being. Lead the CARE Team, or other student support committees as assigned. Conduct outreach to students identified as at-risk for disengagement or withdrawal. Assist with student success, wellness, and retention initiatives across the college. Participates in 24 -hour on call emergency/duty coverage for after-hours emergencies and follow up with appropriate interventions. Other Duties as assigned Requirements: Education and/or Experience: Bachelor's degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs, Social Work, Psychology, Human Services, Counseling, or a related field. Two to four years of experience in student affairs, case management, social services, counseling support, advising, or a related area. Knowledge Skills and Abilities: Skills: Demonstrated ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse backgrounds. Strong communication, interpersonal, and organizational skills. Ability to manage sensitive situations with discretion and professionalism. Demonstrated familiarity with crisis management and crisis/emergency communications preferred. Must have good communication skills both written and verbal and be able to communicate clearly to students, faculty, staff, and vendors. Exceptional attention to detail and ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously. Able to work independently and maintain positive relationships with a variety of constituencies. Must be able to identify complex problems and review related information to develop, evaluate options, and recommend solutions for implementation. Knowledge: Ability to perform basic arithmetic operations (addition, subtraction, multiplication, division) with whole numbers, fractions, decimals, percentages, and measurements, including American money and weight units. Proficiency in using standard office software such as Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint). Experience with Maxient or similar student conduct software. Database and project management skills. Must be detail-oriented and have good data entry skills. Previous case management experience. Abilities: Acknowledges and complies with all departmental SOP, safety, and college requirements. Strong professional ethics and discretion with an attitude of respect for all employed at CoW. Commitment to student development, leadership and teamwork. Additional Information: The College of Wooster does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, sex/gender, gender identity, gender expression, medical condition, political affiliation, religion, creed, ethnicity, national origin (including ancestry), citizenship status, disability, age, marital status, family responsibilities, sexual orientation, veteran or military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, domestic violence victim status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy, or by state, local, or federal law. All offers of employment are subject to verification of the legal right to work in the United States as required by federal law. For more information see our nondiscrimination policy. For more information see our nondiscrimination policy . Application Instructions: For highest consideration please submit a resume, cover letter, and a list of 3 professional references which includes name, telephone number and email address. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation The College of Wooster 536 E. Wayne Ave, Wooster, OH 44691"
    },
    "https://wooster.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203950": {
      "title": "The College of Wooster \n\tJob Posting: Video and Multimedia Production Manager",
      "description": "The College of Wooster\nJob Posting: Video and Multimedia Production Manager The College of Wooster \n\tJob Posting: Video and Multimedia Production Manager Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Video and Multimedia Production Manager Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Marketing and Communications Locations: Wooster, OH Posted: Aug 20, 2026 Closes: Sep 20, 2026 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: Full-time Exempt Position ID: 203950 Share About The College of Wooster: Wooster offers an excellent, comprehensive liberal arts education, culminating in a rigorous senior project, in which each student works one-on-one with a faculty mentor to conceive, organize and complete a significant research project on a topic of the student's own choosing. Through this distinctive program, every Wooster student develops abilities valued by employers and graduate schools alike: independent judgment, analytical ability, creativity, project-management and time-management skills, and strong written and oral communication skills. Founded in 1866, the college enrolls approximately 2,000 students. The College offers a comprehensive benefits program that includes: Health, Dental, Retirement, and Tuition Remission for eligible positions. Job Description: Summary: The Video and Multimedia Producer leads the creation of compelling, distinctive, and inspiring branding video, audio, and motion graphic content that tells the story of the College. Through strategic visual storytelling, this position engages prospective and current students, families, alumni, donors, faculty, and staff while elevating the College's reputation and advancing institutional priorities. This position conceives, develops, and produces creative multimedia solutions that support College initiatives and strategic goals across digital, social, and advertising channels. The Video and Multimedia Producer creates engaging, audience-focused content, measures its effectiveness using analytics, and applies insights to continuously improve future productions. Working collaboratively with colleagues across campus, the Video and Multimedia Producer also manages student interns, coordinates freelance creative partners as needed and helps provide experiential learning opportunities that enhance students' professional development. Essential Departmental Duties and Responsibilities: Produces, shoots, and edits high-quality video and multimedia content for the College's website, social media, digital advertising, events, and other communications channels. Plans and executes all phases of video production, including storyboarding, scriptwriting, scheduling, talent coordination, location scouting, filming, audio recording, lighting, and post-production editing, including motion graphics, captioning, and platform-specific formatting. Conducts interviews with students, faculty, staff, alumni, donors, trustees, and other stakeholders to capture authentic stories that support the College's marketing and communications efforts. Identifies opportunities to create multimedia content that promotes the College, highlights institutional priorities, and increases audience engagement, while collaborating with the marketing and communications team on creative campaigns and content initiatives. Ensures all video content meets accessibility standards through captioning and other appropriate accommodations. Organizes, maintains, and expands the College's digital media library, including finished productions, b-roll, photography, and archival footage, ensuring assets are properly cataloged, stored, and easily retrievable. Develops and maintains efficient production workflows, file management systems, and archival procedures to support ongoing multimedia production. Monitors content performance using analytics and applies insights to improve future multimedia projects and audience engagement. Trains and supervises student interns, providing meaningful experiential learning opportunities while ensuring high-quality project support. Manages relationships with freelance creative professionals and coordinates external production resources as needed.  Oversees the inventory, maintenance, storage, and replacement planning of the College's video production equipment and ensures the College's YouTube channel remains current, organized, and optimized. Stays current with emerging trends, technologies, and best practices in video production, multimedia storytelling, and content distribution through ongoing professional development. Performs other duties as assigned. Requirements: Qualifications: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Education and/or Experience: Bachelor's degree in broadcast journalism, video production, multimedia production, visual production, visual communications, or related field, from a four-year college or university. Knowledge Skills and Abilities: Skills: Demonstrated skill and experience in video shooting, editing and production, from ideation to finished product, as evidenced by a portfolio of work. Track record of producing high-end imagery for use across the marketing and communications spectrum. Experience overseeing or mentoring staff or student interns. Demonstrated project management ability, managing multiple projects at once and working on deadlines. Broad knowledge of social media video content, multiple formats and styles of short-form storytelling. Photography experience and/or drone licensure a plus. Available to periodically work a non-standard schedule to fulfill assigned duties and responsibilities in accordance with college events. Knowledge: Outstanding written and verbal communication skills Ability to demonstrate leadership and exercise diplomacy, professionalism, consensus building, and discretion with college stakeholders High level of proficiency and experience with the Adobe Creative Suite, including but not limited to Premiere Pro and After Effects or other animation tools, like DaVinci Resolve. Abilities: Acknowledge and comply with all departmental SOP, safety, and College requirements. Commitment to the College's mission, vision, and values. Additional Information: The College of Wooster does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, sex/gender, gender identity, gender expression, medical condition, political affiliation, religion, creed, ethnicity, national origin (including ancestry), citizenship status, disability, age, marital status, family responsibilities, sexual orientation, veteran or military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, domestic violence victim status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy, or by state, local, or federal law. All offers of employment are subject to verification of the legal right to work in the United States as required by federal law. For more information see our nondiscrimination policy. For more information see our nondiscrimination policy . Application Instructions: For highest consideration, please submit the following application materials: Resume Cover letter Video production portfolio and/or demo reel List of three professional references, including each reference's name, telephone number, and email address Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation The College of Wooster 536 E. Wayne Ave, Wooster, OH 44691"
    }
  },
